This is dangerous--once you've blinded the dragon with a wand of
lightning, it will no longer respect Elbereth and can attack you while
you're on it.

You're much safer standing on the burned E and waiting for the dragon
to come next to you so you can whack it.

Missile weapons, spells, and attack wands other than lightning/fire
(fire charges are too valuable as E-burners to waste zapping at things
in non-dire straits) can be mixed in, though I also prefer keeping at
least one partly charged /cold in inventory to help deal with eels and
such.



